msgid "MinMaxScaler_description"
msgstr "Scales and transforms each feature individually to a specific range (by default, between 0 and 1). It is ideal for algorithms sensitive to distances, such as neural networks or K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)."

msgid "StandardScaler_description"
msgstr "Tool that standardizes numerical features by removing the mean and scaling the data so they have a standard deviation of 1. It transforms each value using the Z-score formula."

msgid "Normalizer_description"
msgstr "Preprocessing step that adjusts the range of numerical values in your data to a standard scale. It prevents variables with large magnitudes from dominating smaller ones, speeding up training and improving model accuracy."

msgid "warning_msg"
msgstr ""
"If no name is provided, a default one will be chosen, and if no final path is specified, the file will be saved in the initial file's path.\n"
"If no features in negative ranges are specified, they will be ignored."

msgid "danger_msg"
msgstr ""
